# Terraform-local ignores, next to the code they protect. The root .gitignore
# already covers each of them at any depth; this file only makes the rules
# visible where terraform runs.

# Saved plans. A plan resolves every variable, so it is a blob holding each
# provider credential and client secret in the clear.
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.json
tfplan
tfplan.json
plan.out

# Variable files - secret-bearing.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Crash logs (they embed the request that crashed, provider config included)
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Override files: local, unreviewed config that silently wins over the checked-in
# HCL. Never commit one.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# CLI configuration (credentials blocks, mirror config)
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# .terraform.lock.hcl is COMMITTED — it pins the exact provider builds.
